#  Online Course Fee Calculation

## Problem Statement

An online learning platform offers different categories of courses. Each course category provides a different discount on the course fee.

Design the program using the following OOPS structure:

### Abstract Class: `Course`

Create an **abstract class** named `Course`.

**Field:**
- `double courseFee`

**Constructor:**
- Create a constructor to initialize `courseFee`.

**Abstract Methods:**

- `double calculateDiscount()`
- `String getCourseType()`

**Concrete Method:**

```java
double calculateFinalFee()
```

**Formula:**

```text
Final Fee = Course Fee - Discount
```

### Derived Classes

Create the following derived classes:

- `ProgrammingCourse`
- `DataScienceCourse`
- `CloudCourse`

### Discount Rules

| Course Type | Discount |
|---|---:|
| Programming Course | 10% |
| Data Science Course | 15% |
| Cloud Course | 5% |

Each derived class must override:

- `calculateDiscount()`
- `getCourseType()`

Use a `Course` reference in `main()` to demonstrate **runtime polymorphism**.

## Input Format

- The first line contains an integer `courseType`.
  - `1` represents Programming.
  - `2` represents Data Science.
  - `3` represents Cloud.
- The second line contains `courseFee` as a `double`.

## Output Format

Print the following:

- Course type as a string.
- Discount as a **double formatted to exactly two decimal places**.
- Final fee as a **double formatted to exactly two decimal places**.

## Constraints

- `1 ≤ courseType ≤ 3`
- `0.0 < courseFee ≤ 1000000.0`

## Sample Input

```text
2
50000.0
```

## Sample Output

```text
Course Type: Data Science
Discount: 7500.00
Final Fee: 42500.00
```

## Solution

import java.util.Scanner;

abstract class Course {
    double courseFee;

    Course(double fee) {
        courseFee = fee;
    }

    abstract double calculateDiscount();

    abstract String getCourseType();

    double calculateFinalFee() {
        return courseFee - calculateDiscount();
    }
}

class ProgrammingCourse extends Course {
    ProgrammingCourse(double fee) {
        super(fee);
    }

    double calculateDiscount() {
        return courseFee * 10 / 100;
    }

    String getCourseType() {
        return "Programming";
    }
}

class DataScienceCourse extends Course {
    DataScienceCourse(double fee) {
        super(fee);
    }

    double calculateDiscount() {
        return courseFee * 15 / 100;
    }

    String getCourseType() {
        return "Data Science";
    }
}

class CloudCourse extends Course {
    CloudCourse(double fee) {
        super(fee);
    }

    double calculateDiscount() {
        return courseFee * 5 / 100;
    }

    String getCourseType() {
        return "Cloud";
    }
}

public class Online-Course-Fee-Calculation {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int type = sc.nextInt();
        double fee = sc.nextDouble();

        Course c;

        if (type == 1) {
            c = new ProgrammingCourse(fee);
        } else if (type == 2) {
            c = new DataScienceCourse(fee);
        } else {
            c = new CloudCourse(fee);
        }

        System.out.println("Course Type: " + c.getCourseType());
        System.out.printf("Discount: %.2f%n", c.calculateDiscount());
        System.out.printf("Final Fee: %.2f%n", c.calculateFinalFee());

        sc.close();
    }
}
